@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<h1 class="display-4">API Key Authentication Workflow!</h1>

<div class="container my-4">
    <div class="jumbotron bg-light p-5 rounded">

        <p class="lead text-muted">This page describes how the Blazor client and ASP.NET Core API exchange authenticated requests using an API key.</p>

        <div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
            <div class="card-body">
                <div class="row g-3">

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <strong>User Interaction</strong> — A user triggers an action in a Blazor component, which calls the named HttpClient.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <strong>IHttpClientFactory</strong> — <code>CreateClient("ProtectedApi")</code> returns a client configured with
                            <strong>ApiKeyDelegatingHandler</strong>.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <strong>Delegating Handler Adds API Key</strong> — Before the request leaves the client,
                            <code>ApiKeyDelegatingHandler.SendAsync()</code> injects:
                            <br />
                            <code>X-API-KEY: &lt;client key&gt;</code>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">
                            <strong>Request Sent to API</strong> — The HTTP request travels to the endpoint, e.g. <code>GET /api/weather</code>.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">

                            <strong>ASP.NET Core Filter Pipeline</strong> — <strong>ApiKeyAuthFilter</strong> runs before the controller:
                            <ul>
                                <li>If header missing → <strong>401 Unauthorized</strong></li>
                                <li>If header present but incorrect → <strong>401 Unauthorized</strong></li>
                                <li>If header matches server key → filter calls <code>next()</code> and controller executes</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="p-3 border bg-white rounded h-100">

                            <strong>Response Returned</strong> — Controller returns data, HttpClient receives it, and the Blazor component renders the UI.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


.workflow-font {
font-size: 1.25rem; /* Increase overall font size */
}

.workflow-font strong {
font-size: 1.35rem; /* Make section titles slightly larger */
}

.workflow-font code {
font-size: 1.15rem; /* Slightly larger code text */
}
